# Two images are built from the repository root: the cloud runner
# (`runner/Dockerfile`), which reads this file, and the cloud computer
# (`box/Dockerfile`), which reads `box/Dockerfile.dockerignore` instead; the
# API and the worker are built from `server/` and read `server/.dockerignore`. The runner copies only its own
# sources, so everything else is excluded: without this the context would
# carry the git history, the web client, the corpus and the desktop tree.
#
# Exclude everything, then name what the Dockerfile actually copies.
*
!runner

# ...minus what is generated inside it. A developer's local build would
# otherwise ship their `node_modules` into the build context.
runner/node_modules
runner/dist
